Sequence note

The first post was handwritten and received immediate negative voting. At that point, the downvotes could have been ordinary subreddit weather, so the post was deleted and reposted.

The second handwritten post received the same immediate negative voting pattern. This made a simple one-off explanation less likely.

A third version was then produced with LLM assistance, on the assumption that the user's own writing style might be the main obstacle. That version also received rapid negative voting. It was deleted and reposted, and the same voting pattern reappeared.

This sequence suggests that the reception was not primarily caused by handwritten style. Both human-written and LLM-assisted versions encountered rapid negative voting. The more likely object of rejection was the topic/category bundle: ChatGPT, AI-mediated writing, GitHub links, platform-methods claims, and outsider positioning in the subreddit.

Share counts appeared during the sequence, but their meaning is not established. They may represent genuine interest, moderator alerting, private circulation, ridicule-sharing, or attempts to summon reinforcement. Without independent evidence of where the shares went, they should be recorded as unverified off-thread circulation rather than treated as proof of coordination.

Current evidentiary position: repeated rapid negative voting is observed; post-level locking is observed; moderator adoption of "slop" framing is observed; off-thread circulation is indicated but not interpreted.
